      <li>Use the website to infringe the rights of others</li>
      <li>Use the website in a way that could harm WAYGGO, its customers, partners, or service providers</li>
    </ul>
    <p>WAYGGO may restrict or suspend access where reasonably necessary to protect the website, users, business operations, or other legitimate interests.</p>

    <h2>Transportation Requests</h2>
    <p>When you request transportation from WAYGGO, you are responsible for providing accurate and sufficiently complete information.</p>
    <p>Depending on the service, this may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Travel dates</li>
      <li>Pickup locations</li>
      <li>Drop-off locations</li>
      <li>Group size</li>
      <li>Passenger requirements</li>
      <li>Luggage requirements</li>
      <li>Equipment requirements</li>
      <li>Vehicle preferences</li>
      <li>Flight information</li>
      <li>Hotel information</li>
      <li>Event schedules</li>
      <li>Special transportation requirements</li>
      <li>Other itinerary information</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Transportation planning depends on the accuracy of this information.</p>
    <p>If information changes, you should notify WAYGGO as soon as reasonably possible.</p>

    <h2>Quotes and Pricing</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO may provide transportation quotes based on the information available at the time of the request.</p>
    <p>A quote may depend on factors such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Vehicle type</li>
      <li>Passenger count</li>
      <li>Travel dates</li>
      <li>Mileage</li>
      <li>Hours of service</li>
      <li>Route</li>
      <li>Number of destinations</li>
      <li>Driver requirements</li>
      <li>Parking or toll requirements</li>
      <li>Waiting time</li>
      <li>Special requirements</li>
      <li>Availability</li>
      <li>Local operating conditions</li>
      <li>Other itinerary-specific factors</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A quote is not necessarily a confirmed transportation booking unless WAYGGO expressly confirms the booking in writing or through the applicable booking process.</p>
    <p>Prices, availability, taxes, fees, and other charges should be confirmed in the applicable quote, confirmation, agreement, or invoice.</p>

    <h2>Booking Confirmation</h2>
    <p>A transportation request becomes a confirmed booking only when WAYGGO has provided the applicable confirmation and any required booking conditions have been satisfied.</p>
    <p>A confirmation may identify:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Transportation dates</li>
      <li>Pickup and drop-off locations</li>
      <li>Vehicle category</li>
      <li>Passenger count</li>
      <li>Pricing</li>
      <li>Payment requirements</li>
      <li>Cancellation terms</li>
      <li>Special requirements</li>
      <li>Other applicable conditions</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Customers should review booking confirmations carefully and notify WAYGGO promptly if any information is incorrect.</p>

    <h2>Transportation Operators</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO may arrange transportation through independent transportation operators.</p>
    <p>These operators may be responsible for providing:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Vehicles</li>
      <li>Drivers</li>
      <li>Dispatch</li>
      <li>Local transportation operations</li>
      <li>Vehicle maintenance</li>
      <li>Driver licensing</li>
      <li>Applicable regulatory compliance</li>
      <li>Local operational requirements</li>
      <li>Other services necessary to perform the transportation</li>
    </ul>
    <p>WAYGGO may maintain processes for evaluating and coordinating transportation partners.</p>
    <p>However, unless expressly stated otherwise in a specific agreement, WAYGGO does not represent that it directly owns or operates every vehicle or employs every driver used to fulfill a transportation service.</p>

    <h2>Transportation Partner Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>Transportation partners working with WAYGGO are expected to provide services in accordance with applicable law, their agreements with WAYGGO, and the transportation requirements communicated for the assignment.</p>
    <p>Depending on the relationship, partner responsibilities may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Maintaining appropriate licenses and registrations</li>
      <li>Maintaining legally required insurance</li>
      <li>Providing suitable vehicles</li>
      <li>Maintaining vehicles appropriately</li>
      <li>Providing appropriately licensed drivers</li>
      <li>Complying with applicable transportation regulations</li>
      <li>Communicating operational changes</li>
      <li>Providing accurate information</li>
      <li>Meeting agreed transportation requirements</li>
      <li>Protecting customer and traveler information</li>
      <li>Responding appropriately to operational issues</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Additional partner requirements may be established through separate partner agreements.</p>

    <h2>Customer Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>Customers and organizations arranging transportation are responsible for providing accurate information and communicating relevant changes.</p>
    <p>You are responsible for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Providing accurate itinerary information</li>
      <li>Providing accurate passenger counts</li>
      <li>Communicating relevant special requirements</li>
      <li>Providing correct pickup and destination information</li>
      <li>Reviewing booking confirmations</li>
      <li>Meeting applicable payment requirements</li>
      <li>Following applicable vehicle and driver instructions</li>
      <li>Ensuring travelers understand relevant transportation requirements</li>
      <li>Communicating itinerary changes as soon as reasonably possible</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A transportation plan can only be as accurate as the information used to build it.</p>

    <h2>Passenger Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>Passengers are expected to behave responsibly while using transportation arranged through WAYGGO.</p>
    <p>Passengers must follow:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Driver instructions</li>
      <li>Vehicle safety requirements</li>
      <li>Applicable laws</li>
      <li>Vehicle rules</li>
      <li>Reasonable instructions relating to passenger safety</li>
      <li>Rules concerning prohibited or restricted items</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Passengers may not intentionally damage vehicles, threaten or harass drivers or other passengers, interfere with vehicle operation, or engage in unlawful conduct.</p>
    <p>A transportation operator may take reasonable action when passenger behavior creates a safety, legal, or operational concern.</p>

    <h2>Special Requirements</h2>
    <p>Customers should communicate relevant requirements before transportation is confirmed whenever possible.</p>
    <p>These may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Accessibility requirements</li>
      <li>Mobility considerations</li>
      <li>Child transportation requirements</li>
      <li>Service animals</li>
      <li>Luggage requirements</li>
      <li>Sports equipment</li>
      <li>Musical instruments</li>
      <li>Medical or mobility equipment</li>
      <li>Dietary or cultural considerations where relevant to the itinerary</li>
      <li>Other special transportation needs</li>
    </ul>
    <p>WAYGGO will work to understand and coordinate these requirements based on the information provided.</p>
    <p>However, the availability and suitability of specific accommodations may depend on the vehicle, operator, destination, applicable law, and other circumstances.</p>
    <p>Customers should not assume that a particular accommodation is available unless it has been specifically confirmed.</p>

    <h2>Vehicle Selection</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO may recommend transportation based on information such as group size, luggage, equipment, route, travel duration, and itinerary requirements.</p>
    <p>Vehicle categories may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Vans</li>
      <li>Minibuses</li>
      <li>Mini coaches</li>
      <li>Motor coaches</li>
      <li>Other transportation configurations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A vehicle category or photograph displayed on the website may be illustrative and may not represent the exact vehicle assigned to a particular trip.</p>
    <p>The confirmed transportation arrangement should be used as the authoritative source for the applicable vehicle and service requirements.</p>

    <h2>Changes to an Itinerary</h2>
    <p>Travel plans can change. Changes may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Passenger count</li>
      <li>Pickup time</li>
      <li>Pickup location</li>
      <li>Destination</li>
      <li>Number of stops</li>
      <li>Vehicle requirements</li>
      <li>Travel duration</li>
      <li>Flight information</li>
      <li>Hotel information</li>
      <li>Event schedules</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Customers should notify WAYGGO as soon as possible about material changes.</p>
    <p>Changes may affect availability, pricing, vehicle assignment, routing, staffing, or other transportation requirements.</p>
    <p>A requested change is not considered accepted until WAYGGO confirms it.</p>

    <h2>Delays and Unforeseen Circumstances</h2>
    <p>Transportation takes place in real-world conditions.</p>
    <p>Traffic, weather, road closures, accidents, construction, airport conditions, event schedules, vehicle issues, government restrictions, and other circumstances may affect transportation.</p>
    <p>WAYGGO and transportation partners will make reasonable efforts to coordinate transportation in accordance with the confirmed itinerary.</p>
    <p>However, no transportation provider can guarantee that every trip will operate exactly according to schedule under every circumstance.</p>
    <p>When disruptions occur, WAYGGO may work with the customer and applicable transportation operator to identify reasonable alternatives based on the circumstances.</p>

    <h2>Flight Information</h2>
    <p>Where transportation is connected to air travel, customers should provide accurate flight information when requested.</p>
    <p>Flight schedules can change, and airlines may modify arrival or departure information.</p>
    <p>Customers should notify WAYGGO of material flight changes when possible.</p>
    <p>WAYGGO may use available flight information to assist with transportation coordination, but customers remain responsible for communicating material changes affecting their transportation arrangements.</p>

    <h2>Cancellation and Changes</h2>
    <p>Cancellation and change terms may vary depending on the transportation arrangement, operator, date of travel, vehicle, route, and applicable agreement.</p>
    <p>The applicable cancellation and change conditions will be provided in the relevant quote, booking confirmation, agreement, or other transaction documentation.</p>
    <p>Customers should review those terms before confirming transportation.</p>
    <p>If no specific cancellation or change terms are stated in the applicable transaction documentation, the parties should contact WAYGGO for clarification.</p>

    <h2>Payments and Invoicing</h2>
    <p>Customers are responsible for paying amounts due under the applicable quote, booking confirmation, invoice, or agreement.</p>
    <p>Payment requirements may vary depending on:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Customer type</li>
      <li>Booking</li>
      <li>Travel date</li>
      <li>Transportation operator</li>
      <li>Contractual arrangement</li>
      <li>Currency</li>
      <li>Applicable fees or taxes</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Invoices should be reviewed promptly.</p>
    <p>If you believe an invoice contains an error, contact WAYGGO as soon as reasonably possible.</p>
    <p>Additional payment terms may apply to approved business or partner accounts.</p>

    <h2>Taxes, Tolls, Parking, and Additional Charges</h2>
    <p>Transportation pricing may be affected by charges associated with the actual itinerary.</p>
    <p>Depending on the service, these may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Applicable taxes</li>
      <li>Tolls</li>
      <li>Parking</li>
      <li>Venue fees</li>
      <li>Airport fees</li>
      <li>Driver accommodations</li>
      <li>Additional service hours</li>
      <li>Waiting time</li>
      <li>Route changes</li>
      <li>Other charges associated with the transportation service</li>
